    "md5": "64d6aba14d8bc920d993ba9b7130391f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1887,
    "chunk_text": "Lanka, I convey our sincere greetings to His Majesty King Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud, the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques and to His Royal Highness Prince Mohammed bin Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud, Crown Prince and Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.\n\nMadam, I want to emphasize one important point today. That is, these projects are more than concrete, steel and infrastructure; they are symbols of friendship. A road connects our communities; a bridge connects our people; a hospital gives hope to our citizens and a university gives opportunity to our younger generation. Therefore, every road, every bridge, every hospital and every educational institution supported through the friendship of Saudi Arabia represents something much greater. It represents the strong bond between the people of Saudi Arabia and the people of Sri Lanka.\n\nMadam, at a time when Sri Lanka is working to strengthen her economy and create new opportunities for our people, we highly value the continued friendship and cooperation of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia. I believe there is tremendous potential to further strengthen our partnership in education, healthcare, investment, tourism, renewable energy, technology, agriculture and human resource development. We sincerely appreciate the generosity, friendship and development partnership extended by the Government and the people of Saudi Arabia over many decades.\n\nOn this important occasion, I wish the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia continued peace, stability, prosperity and success. May Allah Almighty bless His Majesty King Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud, the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques and His Royal Highness Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman bin Abdulaziz Al Saud and the people of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia! May the friendship between Sri Lanka and Saudi Arabia continue to grow stronger and may it benefit the generations to come!"
  },
