    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24400_english_2026-09-24.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24-0079",
    "chunk_index": 79,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "ebfd482b890c295dc12ab39ff31f9ce6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2110,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Payments for temporary drivers and assistants (as per District Price Committee rates)\n\n\u2022 Other essential operational expenses (Maintenance and servicing costs of water bowsers are not covered.)\n\nWater Allocation\n\nProvision of Drinking Water and Emergency Relief Allocation\n\nIn 2026, the National Disaster Relief Services Centre - NDRSC - was allocated Rs. 12,500 million under Vote No. 1501 for emergency relief, to provide essential assistance to disaster-affected communities, including the supply of drinking water and food - cooked meals and dry rations. For the year 2027, a provision of Rs. 2,000 million has been specifically allocated for the supply of drinking water.\n\nAvailability of Water Distribution Assets\n\nA total of 325 water bowsers, including tractor bowsers, had been handed over to the relevant authorities to facilitate the distribution of drinking water in drought-affected areas.\n\nMonitoring and reporting\n\nRegular monitoring is carried out through weekly and monthly reports submitted by Development Officers (Disaster Relief Services) to District Secretariats and the NDRSC.\n\nAdditional Measures\n\nThe NDRSC continues to coordinate further relief measures in accordance with Government policy decisions to mitigate the impact of drought and ensure uninterrupted access to safe drinking water.\n\nThese measures have been implemented to ensure timely, equitable and efficient provision of drinking water to affected populations, particularly in response to the anticipated impacts of El Ni\u00f1o and prolonged dry weather conditions.\n\n4. Disaster Management Centre\n\nAssessment of duration and severity:\n\nThe Disaster Management Centre - DMC - relies on official forecasts and technical assessments issued by the Department of Meteorology and other competent scientific institutions. The DMC continuously monitors hazard information and undertakes preparedness coordination based on the official forecasts received.\n\n2067 2068\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dda\u0da2\u0dbb\u0dca \u0da2\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dca (\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dc1\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dd2\u0d9a) \u0d85\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab \u0da2\u0dba\u0dc3\u0dda\u0d9a\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]"
  },
