    "chunk_text": "Then, there was a news report in the \"Daily Mirror\" titled \"El Ni\u00f1o: NWSDB has only 100 water bowsers\". So, since you say that the per capita water consumption had been increased from six litres to 15 litres, there would be a delivery problem.\n\nas we are going to have rains and due to other related problems. So, how are you going to address that because your Answer is more in line with the newspaper article that I just read out.\n\nLikewise, Hon. Deputy Minister, if we take the economy-related question of power supply, \"The Morning Leader\" reports \"Power supply: 450 MW power shortfall by Jan.\" These are relevant. That is the reason why we would like to have least-cost power generation.\n\nThen, with regard to inflation, \" The Sunday Island\" of 26th of July 2026 states that there will be an import inflation rather than it being demand-driven. That same thing was mentioned by the IMF team yesterday. I only want to put it in the proper perspective so that you could look into it because that would have a financial impact and that impact should be cushioned so that the people would not be called upon to pay the price through a deficit. I want you to ensure that we would be on top of the situation rather than being forced to bear the additional costing."
