    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24400_english_2026-09-24.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24-0125",
    "chunk_index": 125,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "cd483ab4fd60c048598da6afb04b775d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2019,
    "chunk_text": "It is important, Sir, to understand the true impact of what happens when justice is delayed and who actually benefits when justice is delayed. Though everyday citizens or the normal people in this country experience these delays in ways which fundamentally make their lives unbearable, we know that the delays in the justice system have benefited an elite in this country as well. Generally, what has been the trend? One Government comes into power and starts investigations, which happen in a very lackadaisical manner and not systematically because everyone is part of the whole system and everyone knows that those are merely rhetorical flourishes and none of the investigations ever lead to anything meaningful. Then, that Government changes and a new Government comes into power, and the cases are either withheld or dismissed, and the cycle continues. No one with power or from a political background was ever meaningfully held accountable in this country until these last two years. So, it is only now that we see justice really being applied to all without discrimination.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Prime Minister, you have two minutes left of your allotted time.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd2 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba \u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bae\u0bb0\u0b9a\u0bc2\u0bb0\u0bbf\u0baf) \u0bbf\u0baf) (The Hon. (Dr.) Harini Amarasuriya) Hon. Deputy Speaker, indulge me with a few more minutes, please.\n\nThis has also been criticized. The arguments brought by the Opposition in regard to this Amendment have, at best, been disingenuous and at worst, malicious. We all haveheard the accusations and the aspersions cast upon the Chief Justice in this House as well as outside this House. The Government is being accused of targeting this entire Amendment on a particular individual."
  },
