    "chunk_size_bytes": 850,
    "chunk_text": "Then, when it comes to the question of judicial independence, Sir, which has been raised over and over again during the last few months, we must discuss it honestly. Judicial independence is not protected merely by repeating the phrase or holding up a poster or a placard, but by clear laws, a secure tenure, transparent appointments, adequate resources and respect for court decisions. Sri Lanka has painful examples of what happens when those safeguards fail. We do not have to look far back. In 2013, the then Chief Justice Shirani\n\n2107 2108\n\n2026 \u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db4\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 24\n\nThe current Government enjoys a comfortable two-thirds majority in this House and can easily steamroll its way through Parliament. But, that is precisely what our Government, under the leadership of President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, has sought to avoid, Sir."
