    "md5": "160fb6cc4ad421e3896d31a12c3ab81a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2320,
    "chunk_text": "Thank you very much. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dba \u0db1\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4 \u0dda \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0dca \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dc4\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf. \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da7 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0da9\u0dd2 10\u0d9a \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca \u0dbd\u0dd0\u0d9f\u0db6\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf.\n\n[3.12 p.m.] \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4 \u0db1 \u0dad\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dad\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb0\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Bismillahir Rahmanir Raheem.\n\nMadam, a maximum six-year tenure is introduced for future Chief Justices. The Supreme Court has directed the addition of a proviso, expressly excluding the person holding the Office of Chief Justice from that six-year limitation when the Act comes into operation. My central objection is that this is about institutional independence. I am not making any allegation against any individual judge; I do not question the integrity, qualifications or dignity of the Chief Justice or any other judge, but a perception has emerged to the effect that the Government is acting with an improper motive. Madam Deputy Chairperson, there is a famous idiom or maxim which says \u201cpower corrupts, and absolute power corrupts absolutely\u201d. That applies to this Government, according to the arguments we are placing.\n\nHere, I am not alleging that any judge requested for an extension of tenure. Be that as it may, however, a Constitutional safeguard must be judged not only by the intentions of the people exercising power today, but also by the precedent it creates for governments exercising power tomorrow. Judicial independence is not merely the absence of actual interference, but it also requires protection against the perception of possibility of institutional influence. That is the issue here. So, the crucial distinction between prospective and retrospective application must also be dealt with. If 67 years is the appropriate retirement age, why should it not apply prospectively to judges appointed after this Amendment?\n\n2347 2348\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dc4 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0d9f\u0dda\u0dc0\u0dd3\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db4\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd0\u0dca \u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 25"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-25-2026-09-25",
    "num": "2026-09-25",
    "date_str": "2026-09-25",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-09-25",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24440_english_2026-09-25.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-25-2026-09-25-0166",
    "chunk_index": 166,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "df5efdea00b762f9d78d34904101a361",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1790,
    "chunk_text": "Here, I am not alleging that any judge requested for an extension of tenure. Be that as it may, however, a Constitutional safeguard must be judged not only by the intentions of the people exercising power today, but also by the precedent it creates for governments exercising power tomorrow. Judicial independence is not merely the absence of actual interference, but it also requires protection against the perception of possibility of institutional influence. That is the issue here. So, the crucial distinction between prospective and retrospective application must also be dealt with. If 67 years is the appropriate retirement age, why should it not apply prospectively to judges appointed after this Amendment?\n\n2347 2348\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dc4 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0d9f\u0dda\u0dc0\u0dd3\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db4\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd0\u0dca \u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 25\n\nThen, we observe that the Supreme Court\u2019s own Determination creates an important distinction concerning the Chief Justice. The Court required that the Bill expressly provide that that six-year term limit will not apply to the person holding the Office of Chief Justice when the Act comes into operation. That is constitutionally significant. Why was that transitional provision necessary? Why would applying the six-year term limit to the incumbent potentially raise a tenure issue? Then, may I ask, if changing the tenure of the incumbent Chief Justice requires protection, why should changing the retirement age of other incumbent judges be treated as institutionally insignificant? Does this not demonstrate that changes affecting the serving judicial office-holders require particular constitutional caution? I would dare say that the suggested Amendment by the Court itself demonstrates the importance of prospective protection of judicial tenure."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-25-2026-09-25",
