    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dba\u0ddd\u0d9c\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0bc6\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. (Dr.) Harsha de Silva, you have 14 minutes and your time starts now.\n\n[12.08 p.m.] \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dba) \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dc2 \u0daf \u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bc8\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bb7 \u0ba4 \u0bc6\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbe) (The Hon. (Dr.) Harsha de Silva) Thank you, Hon. Deputy Speaker.\n\nSir, the second point I want to make is, repayments remain heavy, but new financing is thin. Repayments are still high both on domestic and foreign sides. The gross financing need has to be covered every year, not just in\n\n85 86\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dd9\n\none good year. Now, the trend is worrying. For instance, multilateral and bilateral financing has been slow. Listen to me carefully. Leaving the IMF aside, disbursements from other multilateral institutions have been low, and bilateral financing has nearly dried up. In the first half of 2026, multilateral lenders other than the IMF disbursed only about US Dollars 177 million: World Bank, US Dollars 94 million; ADB, US Dollars 52 million; AIIB, US Dollars 23 million and others, US Dollars 8 million. Sir, bilateral lenders disbursed just US Dollars 24 million: Japan, US Dollars 14 million; India, US Dollars 8 million and Saudi Arabia, US Dollars 3 million. By comparison, the IMF disbursed about US Dollars 690 million. So, six months of near-zero bilateral inflows is not a financing strategy. Even if we take today\u2019s Resolution under the Public Debt Management Act, Sir, which relates to the US Dollars 200 million from the ADB, for this year the Government is expected to spend US Dollars 45 million and it is already provided for in the Budget. The Hon. Minister has not even included State banks in the Resolution brought before this House today. So, this is inefficiency. Now, already ten months have gone by and how are you going to spend that? So, these are issues I am bringing to your attention, Sir."
