    "chunk_text": "The third point is, the Public Debt Management Office, which the Hon. Minister was speaking about, has been very slow in deciding how to get back into the international debt market. The IMF Agreement is basically built on Sri Lanka\u2019s ability to get back into the international debt market.\n\nNow, let me make a valid point, which is my fourth point. If you are interested, you can listen. It is about what are called Macro-Linked Bonds, and I am suggesting that\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dba\u0ddd\u0d9c\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0bc6\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. (Dr.) Harsha de Silva, you have two minutes left.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dba) \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dc2 \u0daf \u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bc8\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bb7 \u0ba4 \u0bc6\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbe) (The Hon. (Dr.) Harsha de Silva) Sir, I will get two more minutes from our party.\n\nThe fifth point is, our rating upgrade does not guarantee market access. Yes, we have been upgraded from CCC+ to B-, but that does not necessarily mean we have market access. We need to get, at least, to a BB\n\n87 88\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0dca\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dba \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd \u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dd9\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0d94\u0d9a\u0daf\u0dad\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd 06\n\nrating. Also, you know that only Fitch Ratings has upgraded us and not Moody's or S&P. Therefore, we have to think about the future, what the GDP growth is going to be. Now, they are saying it may be even 3.5 per cent. That is not going to guarantee us an upgrade. This upgrade happened because of what happened previously. That upgrade has to go up from B- to BB or BB+ based on what the Government has in store in going forward."
