    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dba\u0ddd\u0d9c\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dad\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0d82\u0d9c \u0d85\u0daf\u0dd4\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dc4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d87\u0db8\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf. \u0d94\u0dd9\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da7 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dd2 11\u0d9a \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dbd\u0dd0 \u0daf\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dd9\u0dcf.\n\n[1.00 p.m.]\n\nAnd, unfortunately, my Friend keeps asking us, \u201cWhat are we going to do with the bonds?\u201d My Friend, the theory and practical application of bonds are also different. You want the Government to say whether it is going to buy or issue bonds, which is market-sensitive information. He is asking the Government to pre-inform the market about what the Government is going to do with the bonds. That is sensitive information, sensitive data and a sensitive decision. Even the book states that it could be done. We have a great plan as to how to manage our debt. Also, we are very confident about our officers in the Ministry, and we are guided by the relevant authorities to ensure that we would manage this crisis far better than they did.\n\nSir, today, as we speak about this particular Regulation and the change in foreign external outflows, I want to quote one statement, which our Opposition may not have heard, maybe, because it is also in English. It is a statement made at the Seventh Review of the IMF, which states, I quote:\n\n\u201cSri Lanka\u2019s economy has proved remarkably resilient to successive shocks.\n\nThey had clearly stated that Sri Lanka withstood two or three consecutive shocks, but, unfortunately, our Opposition is not willing to understand that. We came out of an economic crisis; we faced Cyclone \"Ditwah\"; we face a global economic crisis, triggering a fuel crisis and we were also threatened by the tariff changes of the USA. So, that is what the world has understood about this country, and they are also very confident that we could manage this debt, we could repay it and our foreign exchange reserves are good enough for us to move forward."
  },
