    "md5": "657d9638b2bf73cdf905cc67ed341d9b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1041,
    "chunk_text": "per cent, out of which the additional increase in revenue from vehicle imports was about 1.2 per cent. That is going to continue into this year is what the statistics are showing because people are still importing vehicles. That is what the Fiscal Policy Department has been doing to succeed in all this over the last two-and-a-half years.\n\nBut, the signal we are giving is that our companies here can now invest abroad, without prior approval of the Central Bank, up to US Dollars 750,000 to meet their investment needs. Even a non-resident who is considered a migrant could repatriate about US Dollars 100,000, the threshold of which was US Dollars 200,000 earlier. So, with approval, we are allowing people to take money out of this country. That is the change which is going to take place, and we have come out of the economic crisis in a very smooth way. If you really look at the review before the last under the IMF Programme, you would understand that they would have warned us, if such a threat existed. But, no such threat existed."
