    "chunk_text": "\u201cNo supplies for Iranian ships: Govt.\n\n\u201cVessels approx. 25 nautical miles offshore, outside SL territorial sea: Foreign Min.\n\nMinistry rejects reports of formal US-SL talks on denying supplies for Iranian vessels\u201d\n\nThen, what did our Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism, the Hon. Vijitha Herath, state in his speech at the UN General Assembly in late September? He described how in March, 2026, Sri Lanka responded to an emergency situation faced by an Iranian ship in distress close to our territorial waters with many sailors' lives in danger. He stated in his speech, I quote:\n\n\"We took the difficult path of navigating a wilderness of sensitivities and marshalling our limited national resources to rescue and look after the wounded and sick.\"\n\nThat was the grandiose statement our Foreign Minister made. The key message in his statement was the thrust on humanitarian assistance, stating, I quote:\n\n\"We saw human lives in danger, and we acted - founding ourselves on international law and on humanity. While safeguarding our neutrality, we placed humanity above all else.\"\n\n\u0d92 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0daf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dd9\u0dba\u0dd2, \u0daf\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1 \u0daf\u0db8\u0daf\u0dc4\u0db8\u0dad\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dd9\u0dcf, I quote:\n\nThis, Mr. President, is the Sri Lanka we wish to bring before the world - a small island nation with a big heart which believes that even in times of conflict and profound division, there remains space for humanity. And that is also what we wish to see reflected in the world. We need a world where our capacity to uphold humanity grows faster than our capacity to destroy it. That is the transformation we should seek.\n\n\u0daf\u0dda \u0dd9\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dda \u0db8\u0dc4 \u0daf\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0d9a\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0dd0\u0db1\u0dca \u0daf\u0db8\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dd9\u0dcf \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf\u0db1\u0dca? \u0dc3\u0dda\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dab\u0daf\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0db8 \u0d9a\u0dab\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0da7 \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0db1 \u0daf\u0dda\u0dd9\u0dbd\u0dd3\u0db8 \u0dad\u0db8\u0dba\u0dd2 \u0dd0\u0db1\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf\u0db1\u0dca.\n\n111 112\n\n2026 \u0d94\u0d9a\u0daf\u0dad\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd 06"
  },
