    "chunk_text": "Then, Sir, I would like to refer to the contradictory economic stand that is being taken by the IMF. I believe that once a country goes into bankruptcy, it is necessary to use the IMF to come out of it, but certainly it does not bestow the right on the IMF to push people beyond the accepted, reasonable limit. The people of this country must be saluted for bearing the brunt of the entire economic crisis of our country. They are the ones who helped us get revenue into this country, going through the difficult period. But, even after all that, when there are only three months more starting by the end of the year to go on with the IMF, we still find them putting conditionalities instead of being part and parcel of the success story of this country.\n\nSir, my concern is that we must cut across the political divide and build a strong economy which would be able to withstand external pressure. We are entering a world of turbulent times, navigating dangerous territories. So, as a result, we must ensure that we beef up our reserves and get investments coming into the country.\n\nThen, take the Free Trade Zone Manufacturers Association. What have they dealt with in the last two years and what suggestions have they made to the\n\n151 152\n\n2026 \u0d94\u0d9a\u0daf\u0dad\u0ddd\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd 06\n\ncountry? We must ensure that the foreign exchange coming into the country is protected. Give them benefits. Is it happening? I call upon the Chairman of the Port City and the Chairman of the BoI, who has just taken over his responsibilities, to ensure that the necessary encouragement, motivation, incentives and relief are provided to them. Instead of just saying, \"We are basically looking at investments amounting to US Dollars 3 billion\", we must ensure that the existing investments are protected. They are asking to improve exporters' tax treatment. Now, this country is overtaxed. There is no point in saying you are collecting money, if you are not spending the money efficiently as well as if we are impoverishing -"
