    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "dbdcbc850d2d507046e430084b7be3d4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1893,
    "chunk_text": "(i) the measures being taken to improve access to local eco-tourism sites;\n\n(ii) whether the Ministry has partnered with stakeholders to upgrade accommodations and amenities;\n\n(iii) the measures being taken to train and employ local communities, particularly youth and women;\n\n(v) the mechanisms for marketing Jaffna globally and domestically, and for monitoring tourism\u2019s long-term impacts on the environment and local livelihoods?\n\n(c) If not, why?\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab (\u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dd4\u0dab\u0dc0\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dab\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dc4\u0dc3 \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0dca\u0d82\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d85\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dba\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf) (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0bae\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bb0\u0bcd) \u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bb5\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0ba3\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0b99\u0bcd\u0bb9 - \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0baa\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b85\u0b95\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. (Prof.) Ruwan Ranasinghe - Deputy Minister of Tourism) Hon. Deputy Speaker, on behalf of the Hon. Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism, I answer the Question.\n\n(a) (i) The Ministry has commenced planning Sri\n\nLanka's \"Global Destination Communication Campaign\" by obtaining\n\n403 404\n\n\u0db1\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dd9 \u0dca \u0dad\u0dd4\u0dcf\n\nconsultancy services under a World Bank-supported project. Under this initiative, plans are underway to develop and strengthen \"Brand Sri Lanka\", implement provincial-level tourism branding for the nine provinces and carry out destination-specific branding for unique tourism products.\n\nThese distinctive tourism products include agro-tourism, coastal and marine tourism, sports tourism, culinary tourism, adventure tourism, meditation and spiritual tourism, wellness and Ayurveda tourism, nature and biodiversity tourism, wildlife tourism and culture and heritage tourism. This Global Destination Communication Campaign is intended to be implemented as a five-year global promotion campaign under the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau.\n\n(ii) Yes."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
