    "description": "Hansard of 2026-10-08",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24467_english_2026-10-08.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-10-08-2026-10-08-0009",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "b1f69cc2c54d2a97afd407e185613b1f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1897,
    "chunk_text": "These distinctive tourism products include agro-tourism, coastal and marine tourism, sports tourism, culinary tourism, adventure tourism, meditation and spiritual tourism, wellness and Ayurveda tourism, nature and biodiversity tourism, wildlife tourism and culture and heritage tourism. This Global Destination Communication Campaign is intended to be implemented as a five-year global promotion campaign under the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau.\n\n(ii) Yes.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority has selected the Kokkilai-Puliyamunai Village in the Northern Province as a \u201cVibrant Sustainable Tourism Village.\u201d This initiative will provide support for community-based organizations, small-scale infrastructure development, livelihood and skill-building programmes, local heritage, tourism products and authentic tourism experiences.\n\n(b) (i) The Ministry incurred an expenditure of Rs.\n\n424 million on 46 projects in 2025 and has allocated Rs. 930 million for 2026 for the development of the tourism sector, including the improvement of access to local ecotourism sites. Accordingly, the details regarding the development projects aimed at improving access to ecotourism sites in the Northern Province implemented in 2025 and scheduled for implementation in 2026 through District Secretariats and local government institutions are submitted in the Annex below.\n\n(ii) The Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority facilitates tourism investors by providing information and guidance on legal and regulatory requirements and by coordinating with relevant State agencies. Furthermore, the Authority collaborates with industry stakeholders and State agencies to raise awareness among tourism service providers regarding the standards and quality requirements necessary for establishing, registering and operating tourism enterprises while also offering them technical guidance and support."
  },
