    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7cf4b314b6c1c9bfed17a7fa28582731",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1660,
    "chunk_text": "(ii) The Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority facilitates tourism investors by providing information and guidance on legal and regulatory requirements and by coordinating with relevant State agencies. Furthermore, the Authority collaborates with industry stakeholders and State agencies to raise awareness among tourism service providers regarding the standards and quality requirements necessary for establishing, registering and operating tourism enterprises while also offering them technical guidance and support.\n\nAccordingly, the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority has agreed to establish five such centres and a letter has been sent to the Vavuniya District Secretary seeking a suitable location in the Vavuniya District representing the Northern Province.\n\n(iii) The nine hotel schools established by the Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management covering all nine provinces channel over 6,000 trained young men and women into the hospitality and tourism sectors annually. Accordingly, the Northern Province Hotel School, which is located in the Jaffna District, channels more than 100 trained young men and women into the hospitality sector each year.\n\nFurthermore, the Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management has been conducting a three-month \u201cHotel Multitasker Course\u201d from the year 2025 for\n\n405 406\n\n\u0dd3\u0dd0\u0dc0 \u0dbb(\u0dca\u0dc4\u0daf\u0da0\u0daf\u0d9a\u0db1)\u0dbb\u0dc0 \u0dcf\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0da7\u0d9a \u0d82\u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc4\u0dc0\u0daf\n\n2026 \u0d94\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dc0 \u0db6\u0d9a 08\n\nthe children of unemployed Samurdhi beneficiary families across the Island under the scheme of \u201cSathkaraye Shramasena\u201d in collaboration with the Department of Samurdhi and private hotel schools."
  },
