    "chunk_text": "2026 \u0d94\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dc0 \u0db6\u0d9a 08\n\nthe children of unemployed Samurdhi beneficiary families across the Island under the scheme of \u201cSathkaraye Shramasena\u201d in collaboration with the Department of Samurdhi and private hotel schools.\n\nFurthermore, the policy includes provisions for adhering to sustainable standards when developing new tourism infrastructure; these measures encompass the promotion of renewable energy use, effective waste and wastewater management and the minimization or elimination of single-use plastics.\n\n(v) As stated in the Answer to (a)(i), plans are currently being formulated by obtaining consultancy services with the assistance of the World Bank for the five-year Global Destination Communication Campaign implemented by the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau - SLTPB. The primary objective of this initiative is to develop and strengthen the \u201cBrand Sri Lanka\u201d and to establish regional branding for the nine provinces. In this process, the aim is to implement destination-specific branding for specialized tourism products, including those related to agriculture, coastal and marine sports, cuisine, adventure, meditation, wellness, nature, wildlife as well as culture and heritage.\n\nIn addition to this, arrangements have been made to host special cultural and culinary festivals to promote the unique culture, traditions, arts, cuisine and historical heritage of the Northern Province and Jaffna.\n\nFurthermore, efforts are being made to successfully showcase the tourism attractions of the Northern Province, including Jaffna, to the global tourism\n\nmarket through national and international public relations and digital promotion programmes which benefit all districts of the Island as well as through the engagement of media, tourism influencers, and content creators.\n\n(c) Not relevant. \u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Rajeevan Jeyachandramoorthy, you can ask your first Supplementary Question."
  },
