    "md5": "a30211e64c93a38143c7ed920b7bbc29",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1860,
    "chunk_text": "Given the structural shift in global trade away from traditional multilateral systems like the WTO and GATT towards aggressive bilateralism, our nation must pivot swiftly to secure vital market access. As a matter of fact, even both the IMF Report and the World Bank Report state the same. In light of regional competitors like India rapidly expanding their Free Trade Agreement network and countries like the Philippines actively securing pacts with the major western economies, we must be smart and ahead of the game. We must aggressively utilize our technical knowledge, domestic capabilities and strategic geographical location to capture the world market.\n\n1. whether the Government has adopted a comprehensive national strategy to expand Sri Lanka\u2019s network of Free Trade Agreements and Preferential Trade Agreements and if so, the countries currently under consideration and the implementation of the road map?\n\n2. the present status, timelines and negotiating strategy for comprehensive Free Trade Agreements or Advanced Trade Agreements with the United States, the United Kingdom, the European Union and Canada?\n\n3. the measures being taken to strengthen the Economic and Technology Cooperation Agreements - ETCA/ECA - with India, improve\n\n451 452\n\n\u0db1\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dd9 \u0dca \u0dad\u0dd4\u0dcf\n\nthe effectiveness of SAFTA and maximize opportunities arising from India\u2019s expanding global trade relationships?\n\n4. following the implementation of the Thailand Free Trade Agreement and the Singapore Free Trade Agreement, the status and timelines for bilateral Free Trade Agreements with China, Japan, Korea, Malaysia and Indonesia?\n\n5. the present status of Sri Lanka\u2019s application to join the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership, including the progress made following the submission of accession questionnaire and diplomatic efforts to secure membership?"
  },
