    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0dc2\u0dcf\u0dab\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dba\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0da2\u0db4\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0d9a\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0baf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9c\u0baa\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0b87\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Shanakiyan Rajaputhiran Rasamanickam) Sir, to get something clarified on this will take an extensive amount of time, but I would not take that much time.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Be very brief, please.\n\n463 464\n\n\u0db1\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dd9 \u0dca \u0dad\u0dd4\u0dcf\n\nHon. Minister, you mentioned that you all were taking certain actions regarding the Chemmani mass graves. However, we have repeatedly stated, on behalf of the victim community, their position, that they have no faith in any domestic mechanism. And especially on Chemmani, why is your Government still hesitant to seek international expertise for DNA testing? You and I both know that the Government of Sri Lanka, the Sri Lankan administration, the police force or any other judicial structure, which the Hon. Minister concerned also confirmed, does not have the expertise to do DNA testing, especially on human remains which may date back to 20, 30 years. So, there is no point in us excavating or exhuming another 500 skeletons with no action being taken on the already exhumed skeletons.\n\nThen, the next issue, Hon. Minister, is about the release of lands occupied by the military. You very correctly said that access has been given to certain areas; the public can now access those areas. For example, the Vasavilan-Palaly Road, which they can travel on, but cannot go to their lands. In Myliddy, Palaly and Keppapilavu, protests have been going on for more than 12 to13 weeks. So, you have to tell us either you are not going or you are going to release those lands."
  },
