    "chunk_size_bytes": 2154,
    "chunk_text": "The Banking Act was amended in April, 2024, strengthening supervisory standards, governance and audit independence for State-owned banks. The parate execution moratorium was lifted in 2025, enabling banks to resolve Non-Performing Loans and expand credit. Private sector credit was expanded by approximately 25 per cent year-on-year by end-2025.\n\nPillar 6 - Addressing Governance and Corruption Vulnerabilities: Achieved\n\n481 482\n\n[\u0dd0\u0dc0 \u0dbb(\u0dbb\u0da0\u0daf\u0d9a\u0db1)\u0dbb\u0dad\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbb\u0dca\u200d\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc4\u0dc0\u0daf\u0dbb]\n\n2026 \u0d94\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dc0 \u0db6\u0d9a 08\n\nPillar 7 - Structural Reforms to Unlock Growth Potential: On Track\n\nAll import restrictions on motor vehicles were fully removed in January, 2025, removing a major impediment to trade and investment. Para-tariff rationalization is ongoing under the World Bank DPO commitments. The Women Empowerment Act was enacted in July, 2024. The MSME support framework has been strengthened through targeted credit programmes. SOE restructuring is ongoing, supported by improved governance and performance monitoring frameworks.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Minister, can you make it brief and mention only the salient features?\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2\u0dba\u0dca\u0dad \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) There are many points to make, but I will just try to summarize, Sir.\n\n(c) The Government acknowledges the challenges and hardships faced by the people of Sri Lanka due to a nation-driven to bankruptcy and the elevated cost of living during the adjustment period. These measures were necessary to restore fiscal sustainability and were not without cost. However, had these reforms not been implemented, the economic situation would have been far worse. The country is now seeing the benefits of these reforms with the benefits of macroeconomic stability and renewed growth being felt directly by the people of Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-10-08-2026-10-08",
    "num": "2026-10-08",
