    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) I have many clarifications to be sought, Sir, within the limited time. But, I will do my best.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Go ahead, please.\n\n487 488\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0db4\u0dd4\u0dca\u0db4\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dda \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bb2\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\n\u0db1\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dd9 \u0dca \u0dad\u0dd4\u0dcf\n\nHon. Minister, I asked this Question owing to certain matters also referred to in the present IMF Report. You mentioned that the economic situation in the country is healthy. But, you would see that pawning, during the past six months, has increased by 128 per cent over last year. For six months, the total pawning has gone up by Rs. 1.1 billion. That is a problem of the people.\n\nThen, the total debt of the country has moved up from Rs. 28.3 trillion in September, 2024 to Rs. 33.6 trillion, as of this moment. That is an increase of Rs. 5.2 trillion in 23 months. You also say that inflation has come down, but it has gone up to 8.1 per cent; food inflation went up by 8.7 per cent.\n\nLikewise, the cost of capital, which was previously at 8.3 per cent, is at 11.3 per cent overall today. It is a 2 per cent increase on the Rs. 33.4 trillion cost that is there. So, the problem that exists is that people basically face ill-affordability in today\u2019s context. You are saying that there is a primary surplus, but that happens because you are not spending on Capital Expenditure. So, as a result, the surplus goes against the primary surplus and then, artificially, you are showing that there is an increase. Hon. Minister, it is not we who are saying this, but it is your information that makes us question you."
  },
