    "chunk_text": "Likewise, the cost of capital, which was previously at 8.3 per cent, is at 11.3 per cent overall today. It is a 2 per cent increase on the Rs. 33.4 trillion cost that is there. So, the problem that exists is that people basically face ill-affordability in today\u2019s context. You are saying that there is a primary surplus, but that happens because you are not spending on Capital Expenditure. So, as a result, the surplus goes against the primary surplus and then, artificially, you are showing that there is an increase. Hon. Minister, it is not we who are saying this, but it is your information that makes us question you.\n\nNow, there is a limited amount of money or scarce resources, and you are allocating those scarce resources to meet the total demand that is there across the country. But, the issue is, you all are not solving the problems, but only increasing the debt of this country. So, Hon. Minister, your Answer has not given the solutions to the problems we have raised.\n\nThe seventh tranche of the IMF has not been approved in toto simply because they see that State-owned enterprises have not been commercialized and the debt-to-GDP ratio - you all are living in the dead past - as of today, is still 103 per cent of GDP.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, come on to your particular clarification, please.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) My clarification is that we are talking of the same statistics. Unlike various other matters which are theoretical in nature, these are not about human rights, but about the living conditions of the people. Hon. Minister, I know you have a bad brief, and you have got to take that bad brief from the little that is there, but please ensure"
