    "chunk_text": "Regarding credit expansion, of course, what matters for the Government with regard to stabilization and moving from stabilization to transformation is Government debt sustainability, and that is on track. Our target is to achieve 95 per cent by the end of 2032, and we have already achieved that target. That is what matters for governance. However, in the economy, in a way, the growth in private credit is also good, as long as it really expands economic activities. To some extent, I agree that private credit may go towards importation, expansion of businesses or maybe towards consumption as well. Also, I agree that pawning may have increased. That is mainly due to some exceptional situations and not due to the prolonged or continuing issue. That is mainly due to the Middle East crisis, which has put an enormous pressure on the prices of food and other items. So, that is the reason.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Minister, make yourself brief please.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2\u0dba\u0dca\u0dad \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) Sure, Hon. Deputy Speaker.\n\nThat eight per cent is just above the inflation target framework of 5 per cent. Then, we will continue with this particular framework for the next three years as well. Our upper bound is 7 per cent and now, it is 8 per cent. We are hopeful that we could maintain a single-digit inflation.\n\n489 490\n\n\u0dd3\u0dd0\u0dc0 \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd3\u0dbb\u0da7\u0dc0 \u0da7\u0daf\u0dad\u0daf\u0db1\u0da7\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc4\u0dc0\u0daf\n\n2026 \u0d94\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dc0 \u0db6\u0d9a 08\n\nThe rise in the cost of capital is also for the time being; yes, it is due to these temporary measures. Sir, we have to give an answer to these. Otherwise, the facts given or highlighted by Hon. Member will be taken as the truth. Then, again- [Interruption.]\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Minister, could you please wrap up? - [Interruption.]"
